welcome back to las vegas now march is  colorectal aware colorectal cancer  awareness month so we caught up with  nevada surgery and cancer care to learn  more about screenings  and of course prevention take a look  march is national colorectal cancer  awareness month  there are about at least 150 000  colorado cancer developed  each year in the country 90 of  colorectal cancer  is completely curable if we screen them  early your family history  your ethnicity play a major role in this  colon cancer health health aspect there  are many tests available  that you can use the two common  tests right now we use our colonoscopy  and a test called color guard everybody  heard about colonoscopy  and know about it it's a endoscopic  examination meaning  i will place the person in sedation  and when you're asleep i place a camera  inside your colon  and visually inspect the colon and if  there's  any abnormality like polyps or growth  that can be removed  so it's a test that is invasive but on  the other hand  the test will be able to remove any  abnormalities that detect it  so in a way it's a test that is  preventive to prevent future cancer it's  also  a test that is therapeutic  that can remove any potential  issues for the future there are people  that  are uncomfortable or afraid taking their  prep work for the colonoscopy  the prep is not pleasant you have to  drink certain  uh medications make you go to bathroom  to clean out all  the residual stew in your colon so we  can have a good inspection  we will work with you to make the prep  as  less uncomfortable as possible so we can  give you a good examination  and you can have your colon health  checked and guaranteed  cologar is a test that's developed by  mayo clinic  if the purpose of that is it's  non-invasive  it's convenient it can be done at home  the  test comes with a kit that after you  discuss with your doctors  the kit will be sent to your home there  are instructions  in the test kit they're pretty  straightforward to follow  you send your proof samples back to the  company  the company will look at it in their dna  analysis  and they will send a yes or no scores to  your doctor's office  then you will discuss with the doctor if  the test came back  as good then you are essentially  clear of the cancer risk for the next  several years you do not need to go out  to do a colonoscopy  and if the test shows some questions  then a colonoscopy will be ordered to  make sure  there's no polyp or cancerous growth in  your body our practice mission  is provide personalized individual cares  to make it easier for you to go through  this difficult time  take the anxiety away from you so you  can focus on your illness  and your health and recover and continue  your life enjoy with your family  contact nevada surgery and cancer care  at 702-739-6467 or visit  nvscc.com
 

